    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2e7658d2-ed56-52f4-aa99-24f6887ca869",
      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 12 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -31 & 0 & 48 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above $a_{32}=-2$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 12 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}+R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 12 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{2}:=R_{2}-4R_{3}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -12 \\\\ -31 & 0 & 48 \\\\ 7 & -2 & -9\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}+R_{3}$ and $R_{2}:=R_{2}-4R_{3}$.",
