      ":question/problem": "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -8 & 9 & -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 23\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form $R_{i}:=R_{i}+kR_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below $a_{22}=-1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -8 & 9 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{1}:=R_{1}-3R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -8 & 9 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n\\xrightarrow{R_{3}:=R_{3}+9R_{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 23\\end{bmatrix}=B\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$R_{1}:=R_{1}-3R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3}+9R_{2}$.",
